{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795303285,"nonce":"W35CHhMyHqd3Nh4n53ELITkw8ns=","title":"The frame rate of a match is lower than before while the shared machine is busy","message":"**What happens.** On 2026-11-21 near 23:20, the solo scenario on the release WebGPU client measured 41 to 47 frames a second, where its limit is 50. The online scenario, with three pages on one GPU, measured 15 to 18 against its limit of 45. Earlier the same evening, the build before the sky and the current build both held 60 when each ran alone, so part of the drop is other load on the machine. The load average stayed near 6 with no busy process of the agent.\n\n**What is known.** Three pages at once draw 29 frames a second with the clouds and 29 without, so the clouds are not the cost. A quarter of the pixels gives only 34, so the cost is in the work of each frame and not in the pixels. The effects of soft puffs, the radar, and the rules are the next suspects.\n\n**Next step.** Profile one page with the performance panel of Chromium on a quiet machine, and compare the build before the sky (commit ec50e60) with main.\n\nAgent: Claude Opus 5.5","files":null}]}